From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 13:57:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] media: iris: allow larger capture buffer pools on HFI
 gen2

Threaded video clients can retain more than 32 decoded surfaces before
returning them to the decoder. For example, VLC using VA-API can request
more surfaces with its default frame threading. The default vb2 limit
of 32 buffers prevents these clients from allocating the capture pool
they need.

Set the HFI gen2 decoder CAPTURE queue limit to
DEFAULT_MAX_HOST_BUF_COUNT, allowing up to 64 buffers. This only raises
the maximum userspace can request; the minimum allocation, OUTPUT queue
and encoder queues remain unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>
Source: https://github.com/radxa-pkg/libva-v4l2/blob/0e4ce1e05da1d0a92b342efc2090b9e4987035e1/patches/0002-media-iris-allow-larger-capture-buffer-pools-on-HFI-.patch
Source-commit: abe302bc460e5014baa43bcf181731c3766392be
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vidc.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vidc.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vidc.c
index 05aab6e3005d..8c96b007b391 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vidc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vidc.c
@@ -140,6 +140,9 @@ iris_m2m_queue_init(void *priv, struct vb2_queue *src_vq, struct vb2_queue *dst_
 	dst_vq->drv_priv = inst;
 	dst_vq->buf_struct_size = sizeof(struct iris_buffer);
 	dst_vq->min_reqbufs_allocation = MIN_BUFFERS;
+	if (inst->domain == DECODER &&
+	    inst->core->iris_firmware_data == &iris_hfi_gen2_data)
+		dst_vq->max_num_buffers = DEFAULT_MAX_HOST_BUF_COUNT;
 	dst_vq->dev = inst->core->dev;
 	dst_vq->lock = &inst->ctx_q_lock;
 
